# Third-party enemy art: Librarium battlers by Ækashics (akashics.moe), used
# under http://www.akashics.moe/terms-of-use/. Licensed for game development,
# but redistribution of the raw files is not permitted, so the 2,169 PNGs stay
# out of version control. See docs/AUTHORSHIP.md §9.
src/assets/enemies/

# Third-party tile art: Epic RPG World packs (Old Prison, Grass Land 2.0 and
# the rest) by Rafael Matos / Mattz Art, bought for this project. Licensed for
# use in a game, not for redistribution, so the packs (and their zips) stay
# out of version control like the battlers above. The composed scenes in
# src/ui/lib/tilemaps/*.map.json are ours (tile INDEXES, no pixels); a checkout
# without the packs draws the node diagram instead. See docs/TILEMAPS.md.
src/assets/tilemaps/

# Third-party icon packs, one folder per source under src/assets/packs/:
# clockwork-raven/ (the full sheet in 64x64/, the Raven Fantasy skill packs,
# Epic Weapons 3, Trees and Logs, and legacy/: the icon folders that were
# committed until 2026-10-22), aekashics/ (the 41 icon sheets that sat in
# combatStyleIcons/), idylwild/ (CC0, kept out the same way). Bought or not,
# no pack pixels go in git, the icons the game uses included: git holds
# src/ui/lib/icons/manifest.json (names and file paths, no pixels), and a
# checkout without the packs shows the emoji. See docs/plans/pixel-icons.md
# and docs/AUTHORSHIP.md §9.
src/assets/packs/
